From 04736fedc4a7e4254fb1e68284cf879ebaf1183e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bateske <kevin@bateske.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 10:36:32 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] CHGfx P4: gfx_blit4k, a keyed word blit at any x with flip,
 remap, ink and dither

Raw 4 bpp frames kept as whole 32-bit words (wWords a row, colour 15 the
key), as art streamed from an SD card into a RAM cache arrives: each row
is funnel-shifted into the framebuffer's words and merged under a SWAR
mask of its opaque pixels, so any x costs the same. GFX_B4_FLIPH mirrors
the padded width, GFX_B4_REMAP recolours (15 stays the key), GFX_B4_SOLID
paints every opaque pixel in GFX_B4_INK(c), GFX_B4_DITHER stipples it
through a 4x4 Bayer matrix anchored to the screen (level 0..16). Clipped
to the clip rectangle on every edge.

Its own file: the setup runs from flash, only the row loops sit in SRAM
(~540 bytes, no calls, the frame pointer kept so -msave-restore cannot
add __riscv_save calls into flash). Images that do not call it are
byte-identical (CHWords, CHWordWheel, CHCrossword checked). Host test
extras/tests/blit4k/test_blit4k.cpp: ~33,000 random cases against a
pixel-at-a-time reference (every x phase, flips, remaps, ink, every dither
level, random clips including empty and one-column ones).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
